WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.508 --> 00:00:05.105
(lighthearted music and whistling)

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.751
- Why are you guys so
obsessed with ranch dressing?

00:00:08.751 --> 00:00:09.751
- Why is it on everything?

00:00:09.751 --> 00:00:13.422
- Pizza does not need
to be dripped in ranch.

00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:14.506
- Why is it called ranch?

00:00:14.506 --> 00:00:16.216
- No American has been able to tell me

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.135
exactly what is in ranch dressing.

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:19.261
- Is it from the ranch?

00:00:19.261 --> 00:00:20.971
Does it contain flavors that you would

00:00:20.971 --> 00:00:22.723
assimilate with a ranch?

00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:25.851
Why does all of your money
look exactly the same?

00:00:25.851 --> 00:00:28.283
- Change it up a little, add
some color, a little flair.

00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:30.714
- It's like a big joke to
fool people when they're drunk

00:00:30.714 --> 00:00:32.284
into tipping more than they should.

00:00:33.401 --> 00:00:35.412
- Who came up with a one cent coin? Why?

00:00:35.412 --> 00:00:36.903
- We got rid of them a million years ago.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.921
I don't even remember one
cent and two cent coins.

00:00:38.921 --> 00:00:39.915
- How much did it cost to make?

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:41.763
It couldn't of cost one
cent. You're losing money.

00:00:41.763 --> 00:00:42.868
- You guys don't even like pennies.

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.214
They drop 'em, they're everywhere.

00:00:45.189 --> 00:00:47.664
- You gotta tell me, why
is your cheese orange?

00:00:47.664 --> 00:00:48.749
- Why is your cheese orange?

00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:51.377
- Seriously, my mom stared at
the cheese for like a week.

00:00:51.377 --> 00:00:53.379
And was like, nah, I don't understand.

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:54.463
- And why is it in a can.

00:00:54.463 --> 00:00:55.547
- And I tried cheese in a can.

00:00:55.547 --> 00:00:56.840
It's disgusting.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.966
It tastes like cheese in a can!

00:00:57.966 --> 00:00:59.134
- Cheese doesn't belong in a can.

00:00:59.134 --> 00:01:00.510
Cream, I get. Cheese, no.

00:01:02.632 --> 00:01:06.016
- Why are your drinks so bloody big?

00:01:06.016 --> 00:01:08.143
- But yet not a car with a
cup holder big enough for it.

00:01:08.143 --> 00:01:09.770
- Your sizes that you serve in America

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:12.108
are actually illegal in Australia.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.275
- Australians do not drink Foster's.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.277
- Why do you all think
that we drink Foster's?

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.695
- Don't believe the advertising, people.

00:01:18.695 --> 00:01:20.197
We don't all drink Foster's.

00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:22.115
- We got bloody VB, mate, we got XXXX.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.473
They're Australian beers.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.787
- Why don't you just add
sales tax to the price tag?

00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:29.956
- Why don't you just add the
sales tax to the price tag?

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:30.875
- Like everybody else.

00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:32.542
- It's so frustrating.

00:01:32.542 --> 00:01:34.628
- In Australia we have a
Goods and Services Tax,

00:01:34.628 --> 00:01:35.712
and it's all included.

00:01:35.712 --> 00:01:37.672
It says $10, it's $10.

00:01:37.672 --> 00:01:39.132
- Don't tell me that it's $12.45.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.343
I don't wanna know that, I
wanna know the real price.

00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:44.721
- Your non-metric system,
whatever you use--

00:01:44.721 --> 00:01:46.389
- I do not understand why you guys do not

00:01:46.389 --> 00:01:47.975
convert to the metric system.

00:01:47.975 --> 00:01:49.768
- If you want to make
math easier, go metric.

00:01:49.768 --> 00:01:50.810
- It's so sweet.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.563
Ten! Everything's tens.

00:01:52.563 --> 00:01:55.190
- And zero is freezing,
'cause that makes sense.

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:56.733
- One meter is a hundred centimeters.

00:01:56.733 --> 00:01:59.528
One mile is like, ah, that many feet,

00:01:59.528 --> 00:02:00.612
just keep going, keep going.

00:02:00.612 --> 00:02:01.530
Yeah, that'll do.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:03.573
- What's with your gun laws?

00:02:03.573 --> 00:02:05.200
I'm neither against it nor for it.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.286
I just, I guess I'm just
a little confused by it.

00:02:08.286 --> 00:02:09.997
- It's crazy easy to buy a gun.

00:02:09.997 --> 00:02:12.878
I went to the Midwest
and I went to Walmart,

00:02:12.878 --> 00:02:14.392
and they just sell them there.

00:02:14.392 --> 00:02:15.794
- I was in Mississippi and

00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:17.796
my friend bought an AK-47 on a whim.

00:02:17.796 --> 00:02:18.755
That was weird.

00:02:18.755 --> 00:02:20.257
- When that amendment was written,

00:02:20.257 --> 00:02:22.468
no one had weapons that
could dispense, like,

00:02:22.468 --> 00:02:24.010
200 bullets a second.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.388
They were muskets that took
like ten minutes to load.

00:02:26.388 --> 00:02:27.889
- What's going on with your gun laws?

00:02:27.889 --> 00:02:29.566
They're nuts. Babies can have guns.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.436
- Why do your pharmacies sell beer?

00:02:32.436 --> 00:02:36.106
- Next to the condoms and
the tampons, there's beer.

00:02:36.106 --> 00:02:37.649
- Why do pharmacies sell beer?

00:02:37.649 --> 00:02:39.025
Why the hell not?

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.611
I think it's fantastic.

00:02:40.611 --> 00:02:42.495
I love this country!

